{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When you go out to war.</b> Scripture juxtaposed the going out to war here to tell you that one who is missing a limb does not go out to war (see Sifrei). Another thing: to tell you — if you have done justice, you are assured that if you go out to war you will be victorious; and so David says (Psalms 119) ״עָשִׂיתִי מִשְׁפָּט וָצֶדֶק בַּל תַּנִּיחֵנִי לְעֹשְׁקָי״ (Tanḥuma)." "<b>Upon your enemies.</b> Let them be in your eyes like enemies — do not have compassion on them, for they will not have compassion on you." "<b>Horse and chariot.</b> In My eyes they are all like a single horse; and so He says (Judges 6) ״וְהִכִּיתָ אֶת מִדְיָן כְּאִישׁ אֶחָד״, and so He says (Exodus 15) ״כִּי בָא סוּס פַּרְעֹה״ (see Sifrei)." "<b>A people greater than you.</b> In your eyes they are great, but in My eyes they are not great (ibid.)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:46.082641224Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}